## Emergency override

`git push --no-verify` skips the pre-push test hook ({% if language == 'python' %}pytest{% elif language == 'nodejs' %}vitest{% elif language == 'go' %}go test{% endif %}). Use only in a real emergency (broken environment that needs hot fixing in `main`). Add a note
in the commit message explaining why.

Routine "tests are slow / I'll fix it later" is not legitimate use.

